# BQ quests [pack=gtit] BEGIN
### Quest Lines ###

## GT Interesting Thing

betterquesting.questline.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§6§lGT Interesting Thing
betterquesting.questline.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=Settle in, then open a shop or explore. Follow vending for trade, wallets and mail, or tools for flight, prospecting, storage and rings. No quest requires gambling or resetting a world.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§6§lTwo Faces of the Cat Economy
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=Start with your welcome chest. Follow the vending branch for trade, or collect coins to explore the portable tools.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.name=§6§lThe Cat Ops Deck
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.desc=Bring the welcome chest from your first login, or a bed if you already opened it. Set a spawn point and light your first shelter.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.name=§2§lUnboxing the Cat's Welcome Kit
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.desc=Keep a bed and a stack of torches from the chest for your first night. You do not need a second unopened gift.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.name=§6§lBuild the Cat Machine
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.desc=Build a five-wide, four-high TV two blocks deep. The controller sits at the bottom centre of the front; fill the other 39 spaces with Neko casings, optionally replacing one with the dedicated ME hatch.%n%nCraft the portable terminal from a screen cover and a shimmering coin. Bind it to an accessible machine, then use it in air while the target chunk is loaded.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.name=§d§lWiring the Cat into ME
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.desc=Fit one dedicated Neko ME hatch in a casing position and connect it to a powered grid. Convert the old vending hatch in a crafting grid first.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.name=§6§lWallets, Import and Teams
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.desc=Physical coins and wallet balances are separate. Check the active account before depositing. Joining a GTNHLib team switches wallets without transferring your personal balance.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.name=§2§lDaily Sign-In
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.desc=Claim sign-in rewards in their tab. Monthly streaks and lifetime totals are separate; a missed day does not erase lifetime progress.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.name=§8§lPaid to Idle
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.desc=Online time is separate from sign-in. The default daily milestones are 30 minutes, two hours and five hours. Return to the page to claim them before the daily reset.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.name=§d§lThe Roulette and Its Pity
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.desc=Have five coins ready for the default normal draw. The shimmering pool uses its own currency. Ten draws still cost ten fees; teammates share pity within a pool. No purchase is required.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.name=§6§lSaving for a Ten-Pull
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.desc=At default prices, ten normal draws cost fifty coins. Show the budget without spending it. Teammates share pity within the same pool.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.name=§3§lThe Cat Post Office
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.desc=Mail waits for you offline. Collect attachments before deleting a message. Enter your birthday in the sign-in tab; calendar gifts depend on the server.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.name=§2§lBirthdays, Festivals, Cake
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.desc=Enter the month and day in the sign-in tab and add anniversaries if you wish. Greetings arrive by mail; you need not wait for your birthday to finish this entry.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.name=§c§lServer Ops Appendix
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.desc=An optional note for server operators: back up configs before editing gifts, sign-in tiers, pools or trade offers. Players need no admin access.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.name=§6§lThe Player's Toolbox
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.desc=Collect eight coins from loot or fishing and keep them. The rod gives you another chance at both ordinary and shimmering coins.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.name=§6§lSixty-Four to One
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.desc=The default exchange is 64 coins for one shimmering coin, but only 56 on the way back. The offers have separate cooldowns. Show one shimmering coin; do not spend it just for the quest.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.name=§6§lThe Fifty-Six Spread
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.desc=The default reverse offer pays 56 coins, eight fewer than the forward price. Each offer tracks its own cooldown; trading back does not reset either timer.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.name=§2§lTake Flight on Steak
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.desc=Wear the core in a general accessory slot. Flight drains saturation first and needs at least six food points. Pack steak before a long trip.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.name=§6§lFuel for Flight
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.desc=The float core draws on saturation before hunger. Hand in sixteen steaks for eight hearty meals; you keep the core.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.name=§6§lThirty-Two Million EU Wings
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.desc=Charge the electric core at LV before wearing it. It stores 32 million EU and uses 128 EU/t in flight. Food can take over when power runs out if you have at least six food points.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.name=§3§lThe Mind's Eye
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.desc=Switch between veins and underground fluids with sneak-right-click. A scan covers 19 by 19 chunks and costs exhaustion. Look for the results in your VisualProspecting map integration.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.name=§2§lFollow the Map
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.desc=Open the map for vein or underground-fluid markers. If nothing appears, check VisualProspecting, its map integration and the selected scan mode.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.name=§d§lLord of the Rings
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.desc=Find any one of the seven functional rings in loot or trade. Wear it in a ring slot to activate it, and keep one of each for Windrider.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.name=§3§lDistant Grasp
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.desc=Distant Grasp adds two blocks to interaction and attack reach per equipped ring.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.name=§c§lIronheart
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.desc=Ironheart raises maximum health by ten hearts while worn.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.name=§5§lDragon's Breath
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.desc=Dragon Breath refreshes fire resistance, night vision, regeneration and resistance while equipped.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.name=§2§lGluttony
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.desc=Gluttony restores food, then saturation. Below five food points it can refill both, with a minute between emergency refills.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.name=§d§lWindrider, the Final Ring
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.desc=Craft Windrider from one of each functional ring and two coins. Wear it for flight without the float core's hunger cost.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.name=§2§lQuests That Unlock Trades
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.desc=Check whether a locked offer needs a quest or is on personal cooldown. Finish the named quest or wait out that offer's timer.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.name=§b§lTempest
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.desc=Tempest grants Speed II and Jump Boost II. Try a short jump before sprinting through a mine.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.name=§6§lMountainbreaker
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.desc=Mountainbreaker grants Haste II for mining and Strength II for combat.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.name=§9§lSkywalk
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.desc=Skywalk raises step height to 1.1 blocks, enough to walk straight up a full block.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIg.name=§b§lTeaming Up
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIg.desc=Open /gtnhteam to join or create a team. Team membership switches the active wallet without moving personal funds. Solo players need not form a team for this note.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIw.name=§b§lReincarnation 101
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIw.desc=Reincarnation starts a new world and is limited to private single-player games. Deposit what you want to carry over before confirming. Showing the crystal is enough here.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJA.name=§d§lNeko Infinity Storage Unit
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJA.desc=One drive bay holds this multichannel unit. Each supported channel has its own contents. An old infinite item cell and fluid cell can be crafted together into the new unit.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQ.name=Neko Dimension Pocket
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQ.desc=Turn your infinite unit into a pocket with 135 base slots. Configure and enable its transfer channels before closing the interface. Pick an upgrade that suits your loadout.
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJg.name=Portable Vending Terminal
betterquesting.quest.R1RJVAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJg.desc=The portable terminal opens its bound Neko vending machine remotely. Inventory and trades stay at the machine. Right-click an accessible machine to bind, then use the terminal in air. Cross-dimensional access still needs the target chunk loaded. Craft an unbound terminal from a screen cover and a shimmering coin; binding another machine replaces the old target. The inventory check accepts both bound and unbound terminals without consuming them.
# BQ quests [pack=gtit] END

