# ★★R98 S2 (request 1 "drastically simplify the tooltip"): the contiguous family was
# <b>renumbered as a whole</b> from 0..9 down to 0..3 — NOT "delete a few and keep the rest",
# because the consumer loop breaks on equals(key) ⇒ a gap silently truncates every later line.
# Where the six removed lines went (R36 "a removed shape must have a new home"), line by line:
#   old .1 geometry sheet → the panel already shows it (135 cells / 18 fluid slots / 72-cell grid)
#   old .2 binding flow   → near-verbatim duplicate of the panel note gtit.pocket.note.summary
#   old .3 powered-cell   → same duplication, plus the runtime readout gtit.pocket.bind.unlocated
#   old .4 NEI ghost cell → five more precise spots on the panel side (ghost.* keys)
#   old .5 cadence        → merged into the appended line gtit.pocket.tooltip.distill_fast (name frozen)
#   old .9 per-slot/total capacity → yielded to the panel's gtit.pocket.fluid.capacity (DP-5)
# The freed rows are handed to the element reserve line gtit.pocket.tooltip.element (six entries,
# all six always print with 0 for empty since R99, appended at the very bottom of the tooltip).
# The three declaration spots survive untouched: new .1 = R39a equal fluid rows,
# new .2 = R53b contents live in the item, new .3 = the one-shot crafting cost.
# ★★R100 slice E (description trim): family 4 → 3 — the R39a declaration row (old .1 fluid
# column direction note) is removed as an explicit reversal (the misreading it guarded against
# has no surface now that every panel column is shaped alike; reversal annotation sits in the
# item class javadoc at the original declaration spot, ledger updated by slice G); the remaining
# rows are renumbered to {0,1,2} and rewritten short and colloquial: .0 how to open /
# .1 = R53b contents live in the item (old .2) / .2 = crafting cost (old .3).
